=== ★★ GUEST PRECONDITION 2 — HOST-SIDE RAM. cup8bench mallocs 3 x N^2 x 4 per size ===
    ⊘ At N=2048 that is 48 MiB of GUEST RAM. If malloc fails it prints 'OOM host' and
      exits 1 — a GUEST-IMAGE failure, not our address plane.
                   total        used        free      shared  buff/cache   available
    Mem:            1967         345        1349           0         419        1622
BENCH_GUEST_MEMFREE_MB=1348

=== push + build in the guest ===
    ⊘ cup8bench.c does NOT include <cuda.h>: it declares the Driver-API entry points it
      uses, so guest and host build it with the same one-line gcc invocation. That is
      what makes the two arms comparable at all.
BENCH_GCC_RC=0
